    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "1. Since it is stated at bar by the learned counsel for the petitioner that the lis involved in the instant writ petition is squarely covered by a decision made in \"Indore Development Authority v/s Manoharlal and Ors.\", reported in (2020)8 SCC 129.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 596,
      "end": 844,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Indore Development Authority v/s Manoharlal and Ors.\", reported in (2020)8 SCC 129",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 761,
          "end": 843
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "In view of this, both contingencies as required under Section 24(2) of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in lands Acquisition,\nRehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 have been complied with therefore, there is no lapsing.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 845,
      "end": 1083,
